          hints: [String.raw`Start with the characteristic equation and its discriminant. Which of the three cases is it?`, String.raw`$r^2 + 5r + 6 = 0$ has $D = 1$: two real roots. Write $y = C_1e^{r_1t} + C_2e^{r_2t}$, differentiate, and use both initial conditions.`, String.raw`$r = \frac{-5 \pm 1}{2}$ gives $r = -2, -3$. Then $C_1 + C_2 = 2$ and $-2C_1 - 3C_2 = -5$.`],
